# Stopping a protecting service through another service manager (SysV init
# scripts, `invoke-rc.d`, OpenRC, runit) is read as `systemctl stop` of the
# same unit, and turning one off at boot (`rc-update del`, `update-rc.d
# disable`, `chkconfig off`) as `systemctl disable`; `service` verbs that
# empty or unload a protection are a stop. Stopping or restarting any other
# service stays safe.
