# systemctl verbs that change many units at once or a unit's own file:
# `isolate` stops every unit the target does not want, `set-default` to a
# target other than the graphical or multi-user one boots into it,
# `preset-all` enables and disables units by the preset files, and `edit`,
# `revert` and `preset` of a protecting unit change how it runs. A `--user`
# isolate changes only the user's own session, so it is safe.
posix safe | systemctl get-default
posix safe | systemctl set-default graphical.target
posix safe | systemctl set-default multi-user.target
